				<r3d:description language="eng">DSpace@MIT is a service of the MIT Libraries to provide MIT faculty, researchers and their supporting communities stable, long-term storage for their digital research and teaching output and to maximize exposure of their content to a world audience.
DSpace@MIT content includes conference papers, images, peer-reviewed scholarly articles, preprints, technical reports, theses, working papers, research datasets and more.  This collection of more than 60,000 high-quality works is recognized as among the world&#039;s premier scholarly repositories and receives, on average, more than 1 million downloads per month.</r3d:description>
